C-PHY: the trios go in the ODD bits, not in 0x07

Patch 0089 removed the clock lane bit and left ctrl5 = 0x07 for three trios.
Measured on the phone: ctrl5 = 0x07, lane_mask = 0x07, and zero packets.

It was wrong. The vendor driver computes the trio enable like this
(cam_csiphy_core.c, csiphy_3phase branch):

    lane_mask = csiphy_dev->csiphy_info.lane_mask & LANE_MASK_3PH;
    mask = lane_mask;
    while (mask != 0) {
            temp = (i << 1) + 1;
            lane_enable |= ((mask & 0x1) << temp);
            mask >>= 1;
            i++;
    }

that is, bit 2i+1 for each trio. For three trios: bits 1, 3 and 5 -> 0x2A.

Contrast it with the D-PHY branch of the same file:

    lane_enable |= 0x1 << (i<<1);        /* EVEN bits, 2i */
    ... and 0x80 for the clock lane

THE TRIOS GO INTERLEAVED between the D-PHY lane positions, not in the same ones.
0x07 sets bits 0, 1 and 2, which in D-PHY are "lane 0" and two positions that in
C-PHY mean nothing.

Found by reading the vendor code, without spending a single build cycle. In the
same pass two other leads were ruled out by reading:

  - cam_csiphy_cphy_data_rate_config() is a no-op at 2,6 Gbps: its first step
    writes the same values as the base table.
  - the MIPI switch multiplexes CSIPHY1 between the FRONT camera and the
    wide-angle one; the rear camera is on CSIPHY0 and does not go through
    there. A comment of my own in the S5K3T2 driver itself said so.
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c
@@ -1514,9 +1514,23 @@
 	 * fases. Lo correcto para tres trios es 0x07.
 	 */
 	if (cfg->cphy) {
+		/*
+		 * Los trios NO ocupan las mismas posiciones que los carriles
+		 * de D-PHY: van INTERCALADOS entre ellas. Qualcomm lo calcula
+		 * asi, con temp = (i << 1) + 1:
+		 *
+		 *     while (mask != 0) {
+		 *             temp = (i << 1) + 1;
+		 *             lane_enable |= ((mask & 0x1) << temp);
+		 *             mask >>= 1; i++;
+		 *     }
+		 *
+		 * o sea bits IMPARES 2i+1, mientras que D-PHY usa los PARES
+		 * 2i mas el 7 del reloj. Para tres trios sale 0x2A, no 0x07.
+		 */
 		val = 0;
 		for (i = 0; i < c->num_data; i++)
-			val |= BIT(c->data[i].pos);
+			val |= BIT(c->data[i].pos * 2 + 1);
 	} else {
 		val = CSIPHY_3PH_CMN_CSI_COMMON_CTRL5_CLK_ENABLE;
